LinkedList is a class in Java that implements the List and Deque interface and is part of the Java Collections Framework.
  It is a doubly-linked list implementation, which means that each element in the list has a reference to both the previous and next elements.
  This allows for efficient insertion and deletion of elements at both ends of the list, as well as in the middle of the list.
LinkedList is not array based, instead it is node based, where each node contains the data and references to the next and previous nodes in the list.

Each node in a LinkedList contains three components:
class Node<E> {
    E item;        // data
    Node<E> prev;  // previous node
    Node<E> next;  // next node
}

